{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "Black Heron",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/jlipak/black-heron",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "BH/code_quality/P2",
              "name": "code_quality-P2",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "code_quality lens, severity P2"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "BH/code_quality/P1",
              "name": "code_quality-P1",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "code_quality lens, severity P1"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "BH/governance/P1",
              "name": "governance-P1",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "governance lens, severity P1"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "BH/code_quality/P2",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "ALL_LENSES registry maps blind_spot to a function with a different signature than the other three lenses, yet it is stored in the same dict with no type-level distinction, making it callable with the wrong arguments if any caller iterates the dict uniformly."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/black_heron/lenses/__init__.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "confidence": 0.7,
            "lens": "code_quality",
            "severity": "P2",
            "why_it_matters": "The comment documents the hazard but the design relies on every caller knowing to special-case blind_spot; a single `for name, fn in ALL_LENSES.items(): fn(ctx, client, tracker)` loop would crash or silently pass wrong args at runtime.",
            "verifier_note": "Real design hazard but theoretical (no caller in repo iterates uniformly); downgraded to P2 as the bundle excerpt acknowledges the signature mismatch is intentional."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "BH/code_quality/P1",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The run functions in code_quality.py, governance.py, and drift.py are near-identical (same structure, same MODEL, same API call pattern), differing only in the SYSTEM prompt string, constituting significant code duplication across three files."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/black_heron/lenses/code_quality.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "confidence": 0.95,
            "lens": "code_quality",
            "severity": "P1",
            "why_it_matters": "Three copies of the same 10-line function body means any change to the API call pattern (e.g., adding temperature, retry logic, or structured output) must be made in three places, increasing the risk of inconsistency.",
            "verifier_note": "Evidence supports the duplication claim and the maintenance burden is concrete."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "BH/code_quality/P2",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "parse_findings uses `text.find(\"{\")` and `text.rfind(\"}\")` to extract JSON, which will silently produce corrupt JSON if the LLM output contains multiple top-level JSON objects or prose with curly braces before/after the intended payload."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/black_heron/lenses/_common.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 30
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "confidence": 0.75,
            "lens": "code_quality",
            "severity": "P2",
            "why_it_matters": "If the LLM wraps its JSON in markdown fences containing braces or emits explanatory prose with braces, the extracted substring may span unrelated brace pairs, causing json.loads to fail or parse a malformed object.",
            "verifier_note": "Real fragility but confidence below P1 floor; downgrade to P2."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "BH/code_quality/P1",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "check_evidence_in_context only searches sample_files and entry_points but not the file_listing or git_log_recent, so findings that cite evidence from git commit messages (which are part of the prompt sent to the LLM) will be incorrectly flagged as evidence-not-in-bundle."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/black_heron/evidence_verifier.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 35
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "confidence": 0.9,
            "lens": "code_quality",
            "severity": "P1",
            "why_it_matters": "The drift lens explicitly asks the LLM to cite commit messages as evidence; if git_log_recent is not in the haystack, valid drift findings will be marked evidence_in_bundle=false and the verifier will have a strong prior to reject them.",
            "verifier_note": "Concrete asymmetry between what is sent to LLM versus what is checked for evidence presence; affects drift findings systematically."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "BH/code_quality/P1",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The MCP server registration hardcodes \"command\": \"py\" which only works on Windows; on Linux/macOS the Python launcher is typically `python3`, making the installed MCP config non-functional on those platforms."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/install-mcp.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 42
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "confidence": 0.92,
            "lens": "code_quality",
            "severity": "P1",
            "why_it_matters": "The script already detects the correct Python interpreter (`for cand in py python3 python`) but then ignores that detection and hardcodes \"py\" in the JSON output, breaking cross-platform portability.",
            "verifier_note": "Clear portability bug supported by the cited line."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "BH/code_quality/P1",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The jq fallback regex for extracting content only captures the first match of `content` or `new_string` and uses a non-greedy pattern `[^\"]*` that will silently truncate any content containing escaped quotes, allowing secrets in later portions of the string to bypass the scan."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/hooks/scan-secrets.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 20
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "confidence": 0.82,
            "lens": "code_quality",
            "severity": "P1",
            "why_it_matters": "If the written content contains escaped double quotes (common in code files), the regex match terminates early, and secret patterns after the first escaped quote are never scanned \u2014 this is a security bypass in the secret-scanning hook.",
            "verifier_note": "Real security gap but it is a fallback path (jq is the primary); downgraded from P0 to P1 since severity floor for P0 requires conf \u2265 0.85 and exploitability depends on jq being absent."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "BH/governance/P1",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The evidence-presence verifier uses hardcoded thresholds (`len(needle) < 20` and `needle[:60]`) with no citation to a rubric field, spec, or prior-art justification for why 20 characters and 60-character prefix were chosen."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/black_heron/evidence_verifier.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 36
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "confidence": 0.85,
            "lens": "governance",
            "severity": "P1",
            "why_it_matters": "These thresholds directly affect whether fabricated evidence is caught or missed \u2014 a security-relevant code path whose tuning parameters should be traceable to a versioned policy or documented rationale.",
            "verifier_note": "Despite the evidence_in_bundle=false flag, the cited file is the same evidence_verifier.py that finding 5 keeps; the magic-number governance concern is consistent with the verifier's design and is verifiable from the same source."
          }
        }
      ],
      "originalUriBaseIds": {
        "%SRCROOT%": {
